sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.0 nm on Chrysomallon squamiferum (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Chrysomallon squamiferum (Holocene extant, 0 Ma) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Chrysomallon squamiferum (Holocene extant, 0 Ma) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/chrysomallon_squamiferum_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Chrysomallon squamiferum (Holocene extant, 0 Ma); environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Iron-sulfide sclerites (Warén 2003) and multilayer armor mechanics (Yao 2010) | Turing wavenumber selection (Turing 1952) and Schnakenberg kinetics (1979) | Greigite cubic cell near 0.988 nm (Skinner, Erd and Grimaldi 1964); reconstructed_in_script: Onset k_c solved for D_u at λ=2.0 nm and one IMEX Schnakenberg integration | Activator painted on the MNHN-IM-2000-30072 sclerite mask; transfer_boundary: No source measures a 2.0 nm pigment stripe on this snail. 2.0 nm is the assigned detail-scale wavelength, about two greigite cells.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Yao et al. 2010 stated a reaction-diffusion equation | Does not claim the Pass 1 PDE peak equals 2.0 nm | Does not claim a successor chronospecies after the Holocene animal]; other sources: Greigite, the thio-spinel of iron; a new mineral <https://pubs.geoscienceworld.org/msa/ammin/article/49/5-6/543/54000>; phenomenon_size: 2.5 nm (2.5e-09 m, log10=-8.602 m, tier=1_molecular_nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 2.5 nm to 883 nm): 2.5 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-vertex-packing, 2.5 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-bioelectric-polarity, 20 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength, 39 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-clock-wavefront, 88 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-morphogen-condensation, 108 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-elastic-buckling, 123 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-flux-canalization, 172 nm:chrysomallon-squamiferum-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-15522-3>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0912988107>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1093/mollus/eyv013>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/zoj.12279>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1087696> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-chrysomallon-squamiferum-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

